-------AGILE--------
1a.As a vanilla git power-user that has never seen GiggleGit before, I want to…
    quickly understand GiggleGit’s differences from Git, so that I can start using it efficiently without disrupting my existing workflow.
1b.As a team lead onboarding an experienced GiggleGit user, I want to…
    be able to seamlessly integrate them into our current workflow.

2. As a brand new user to git and GiggleGit in general, I want to be able to have a wide selection of memes suited to my tastes to choose from whenever I merge.
    Task: Curate meme selection based on user preferences
      Ticket 1: Get initial user preferences:
        Details: On first startup, prompt users choose their most liked memes out of a selection and store these preferences in a sqlite database for future customization.  
      Ticket 2:  Show similar memes each time they merge:
        Details: Implement a tagging system for memes. Use an algorithm show multiple memes with varying match percentages based on the user's stored preferences to choose from each time they merge.

3:As a user I want to be able to authenticate on a new machine 
    This is more of a requirement or a feature than a user story.  It doesn't say what type of user they are, how they want the feature to behave, the goal of it, or any other sort of personalization. 
    Something like this is more of a user story: "As someone who uses multiple machines, I want to be able to log onto each of them easily so I can access my account without hassle."
